# Director of Realms Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 Joel Bondoux. All rights reserved.

Director of Realms, including its code, documentation, bundled media, and other original assets
(the “Software”), is proprietary software owned by the copyright holder.

## Personal use and monetized streaming

The copyright holder grants every legitimate recipient, at every free or paid tier, a
non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and use the Software in a personal Foundry
Virtual Tabletop instance. Normal player access to a game hosted by that recipient is permitted.

Every legitimate recipient may also create, broadcast, publish, and monetize live streams,
recordings, edited episodes, and clips of actual-play sessions that use the Software. This includes
revenue from advertising, sponsorships, subscriptions, memberships, donations, tips, and platform
payouts. A stream or recording may show the Software's interface and bundled assets as they
normally appear during play. This streaming licence is included in every tier, including Free, and
does not require Patreon verification.

Charging viewers for, or earning revenue from, session streams and recordings is covered by this
streaming licence. Charging players or clients for game-mastering services is paid game-mastering
and requires the broader commercial-use licence below. Streamers remain responsible for player
consent and for all rights in music, game systems, artwork, voices, and other third-party material.

## Beheaded & Banished broader commercial use

A member with an active, verified **Beheaded & Banished** entitlement receives an additional
non-exclusive, non-transferable commercial-use licence while that entitlement is
verified by Patreon or an authorised Director of Realms licensing service. That licence permits
the member to use the Software to:

- provide paid game-mastering services;
- help create and sell original adventures, maps, handouts, and similar works, subject to the
  rights and terms that apply to every input, provider, model, ruleset, and third-party asset.

Manual tier selection or a testing flag does not grant these broader commercial rights. The
broader commercial-use licence ends when the qualifying membership or verified entitlement ends.
Original works lawfully created during an active entitlement may remain published or on sale, but
new paid game-mastering or new commercial products made with the Software require a current
entitlement. Monetized session streams and recordings remain permitted under the all-tier grant
above.

## Rights not granted

The personal-use, streaming, and broader commercial-use licences do not permit anyone to copy,
modify, distribute, sublicense, resell, rent, host as a service, or white-label the Software or its
source code and bundled assets. These restrictions do not prevent normal player access to a
Foundry game hosted by the licensed user or the ordinary display of the Software during a permitted
stream or recording. Any additional right requires prior written permission from the copyright
holder.

The Software does not grant rights in third-party assets or guarantee that generated output is
available for commercial use. The user is responsible for complying with all applicable provider,
model, asset, game-system, and other third-party terms.

